  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing at the Buskirk-Chumley Theatre in Bloomington, Indiana, on Saturday, June 15, 2013 [1][2]. The setlist features nineteen songs, including rare tracks like “Pure Gold” and “Cutter,” which have limited archival history [1][2]. Notable highlights include “In the Hidden Places,” a bustout appearing for the first time in 79 archived shows after a 2356-day hiatus [1][2]. The performance also includes “Song for Dana Plato,” a rare and bustout track, and “Terror Song,” another bustout with a 2913-day gap since its last appearance [1][2]. The recording is presented in FLAC format and was captured using the built-in microphones on a Zoom H2 recorder [1]. The audio was normalized and track-split in Sound Studio [1]. This show is part of the Tuttlingen Warriors tour, a duo configuration featuring John Darnielle and Peter Hughes [1]. The uploader notes that the performance included spoken introductions and stories related to “Dumb people/Alpha Rats Nest” and the Tuttlingen Warriors [1]. This is the 187th show in the archive’s collection for the performer, following a previous archived show at the Taft Theatre Ballroom on June 14, 2013 [2]. The recording provides a complete view of the evening’s musical and spoken content [1].",
